{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927966-precognition-new-supernatural-merit","id":927966,"title":"Precognition (New Supernatural Merit)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-07T21:46:34-07:00","id":927966,"title":"Precognition (New Supernatural Merit)","content":"This is a new Supernatural Merit I came up with and wanted to share. I don't know if there already is a Precognition merit out there somewhere, I'm new to Chronicles and have only read CofD and VtR. I think this power might be a little bit OP, as I have no practice balancing new abilities yet, so if if you can think of a way to improve it feel free to let me know. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernatural Merit:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Precognition (1 Dot to 5 Dots)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Composure 3 Dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: Your character has a limited capacity to see glimpses of the future, usually only in the next few seconds. This has a variety of uses depending on how practiced the character is controlling it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Threat Forecast (1 Dot)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can focus your precognition on scanning the future for any sense of danger to yourself or a small group of people you are physically close to. First, spend 1 Willpower. For the rest of the scene, you gain +3 to Perception rolls to notice stealth or hostile activity. In addition, if there are any nearby foes actively preparing or considering attacking you or your group, you are alerted by a sourceless sense of anxiety and cold sweat. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dowsing (2 Dots)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By scanning the futures in which your character searches for something, you can steadily narrow down its physical location. Start by deciding on the target you are searching for. It must be a person or physical object, and your character must have seen it or interacted with it before (seeing a photo of it works). Then, spend 1 Willpower. Each time you move at least 30 yards in a specific direction, the Storyteller will inform you whether your character feels they are getting &quot;warmer&quot; (closer) or &quot;colder&quot; (further away). The target you are seeking must be within a mile or so, or you will only feel a vague uncertainty.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fore-action (3 Dots)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character is now practiced enough with their foresight to gain split-second flashes of future sight, just enough to act immediately when something goes wrong. To an outside observer, it appears as though you have super-human reflexes, but in actuality you are simply moving at the exact moment things begin to get dangerous. At the start of a fight, you may spend 1 Willpower to immediately jump to the top of the Initiative list for your first action. After the first round, use your ordinary Initiative position instead. Outside of a fight, you can use this to react to a sudden environmental hazard such as an explosion, falling debris, or an out-of-control speeding car. If the hazard is something that could be reasonably avoided by moving within your regular Speed, you may spend 1 Willpower to automatically avoid it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Temporal Sentry (4 Dots)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can enter into a meditative trance, during which you cannot do anything else, and your trance is broken if you are distracted in anyway by an outside source. Spend 1 Willpower. The trance lasts up to 3 hours. Extending the trance beyond 3 hours requires periodic (every 30 minutes) Resolve + Composure rolls to maintain it. While in the trance, your character watches the myriad possible futures for the approach of any outsiders, keeping track of an area about the size of a large house. If anyone, hostile or otherwise, approaches the area you are watching, roll Resolve + Composure. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure: The sensory overload is too much for you, and you break out of the trance without learning anything useful. Take the Spooked or Shaken condition. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure: With so much information being parsed, you fail to notice the approaching target, and they slip into your area while you are still in your trance. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success: You have forewarning that someone is approaching, including their appearance and body language. You have about a minute before they approach, and may end the trance and act whenever you wish. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success: Same as success, except you have about 5 minutes of time to prepare for their approach.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Future Casting (5 Dots)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You have gained exceptional control of your future sight, able to divine the exact outcomes of future actions. First, spend 1 Willpower. Then, decide a single simple action to take. In a fight, or an equivalent dangerous situation where every second counts, this amounts to a single Instant Action and its immediate outcome. Outside of a fight, you can perform a simple action that takes about 5 minutes, such as a short conversation. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Once the outcome is decided, including all dice rolls, you may decide whether to accept the outcome as it has been seen, in which case nothing changes. If you do not like the outcome, you may declare that everything that occurred was your future vision and that you would like to do something else. Spend another Willpower, and you may make a different action as normal. You retain all information learned during your future casting. This can be exceptionally useful in a myriad of ways. For instance, you could accuse a suspected traitor of falsehood to see their reaction, then reverse it so they do not know you are on to them. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:16:37-07:00","id":928146,"title":"","content":"So you are structuring it like a Style merit?<br /> <br /> Hmm. I might break out some of the effects into other merits, which would require the base Precognition.<br /> <br /> Base effect might be your first ability, or a general Initiative bonus for the first/surprise round.<br /> <br /> Also, most mortal Supernatural Merits come with some kind of downside. For this, I could see a Condition, much like with Omen Sensitivity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T19:50:14-07:00","id":931149,"title":"","content":"I really like this now that I read through the whole thing. The 5 dot version seems like it could be really fun, but also possibly game derailing for some storytellers that have a secret they hope to reveal in a dramatic way. I would suggest you make the last part give more vague answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}